1
00:00:00,759 --> 00:00:03,313
[logo buzzes]

2
00:00:31,962 --> 00:00:36,795
[dark, unsettling
music building]

3
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:45,459
<i>[woman]: I'm not safe in here.</i>

4
00:00:52,017 --> 00:00:54,675
<i>I feel like I'm being watched.
Like...</i>

5
00:00:57,988 --> 00:01:00,163
<i>...there's eyes on me.</i>

6
00:01:07,791 --> 00:01:09,793
I'm so scared.

7
00:01:16,973 --> 00:01:18,699
[video glitches]

8
00:01:19,838 --> 00:01:22,634
[unintelligible audio]

9
00:01:26,983 --> 00:01:29,330
[thunderous bang]

10
00:01:29,434 --> 00:01:33,265
[people struggling and arguing]

11
00:01:37,269 --> 00:01:39,892
[arguing calms]

12
00:01:39,996 --> 00:01:42,447
[footsteps thumping]

13
00:02:14,375 --> 00:02:16,446
[door creaks open]

14
00:02:39,676 --> 00:02:43,232
[footsteps thump]

15
00:02:43,335 --> 00:02:45,682
[Riley]: Mia!

16
00:02:45,786 --> 00:02:47,684
[wild animals howling]

17
00:02:49,341 --> 00:02:51,274
[ominous growl]

18
00:02:56,037 --> 00:02:57,729
[gloomy music plays]

19
00:02:57,832 --> 00:02:59,938
<i>[Reporter]: The hosts of
the popular YouTube channel</i>

20
00:03:00,041 --> 00:03:03,079
<i>"Paranormal Paranoids" have now
been missing for a week.</i>

21
00:03:03,183 --> 00:03:05,219
<i>[Reporter 2]: Speculation
abounds for the whereabouts</i>

22
00:03:05,323 --> 00:03:07,117
<i>of the so-called
"Paranormal Paranoids."</i>

23
00:03:07,221 --> 00:03:09,465
<i>Peter Bailey, Laura Tucker,</i>

24
00:03:09,568 --> 00:03:11,536
<i>David Reynolds,
and Riley Brennan.</i>

25
00:03:11,639 --> 00:03:13,262
<i>[Reporter 3]: They were last
week near the southern edge</i>

26
00:03:13,365 --> 00:03:14,470
<i>of Darke County, Ohio,</i>

27
00:03:14,573 --> 00:03:17,404
<i>near an abandoned town
called Shelby Oaks.</i>

28
00:03:17,507 --> 00:03:18,784
<i>[Reporter 4]: The Darke County
Police Department say</i>

29
00:03:18,888 --> 00:03:20,303
<i>they're doing their best
to locate them,</i>

30
00:03:20,407 --> 00:03:21,580
<i>but have very few leads.</i>

31
00:03:21,684 --> 00:03:23,306
<i>- These people are fakers, man.</i>

32
00:03:23,410 --> 00:03:24,756
They've always been frauds.

33
00:03:24,859 --> 00:03:25,757
<i>They're still frauds.</i>

34
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:27,379
<i>- They're baiting you.</i>

35
00:03:27,483 --> 00:03:28,449
Just building anticipation
for the next episode.

36
00:03:28,553 --> 00:03:31,832
<i>- They recently started
using two cameras.</i>

37
00:03:31,935 --> 00:03:33,868
<i>The cops have one.</i>

38
00:03:33,972 --> 00:03:34,524
So, where's the other?

39
00:03:34,628 --> 00:03:36,354
<i>- The parents are requesting</i>

40
00:03:36,457 --> 00:03:38,459
<i>that the public take
this seriously.</i>

41
00:03:38,563 --> 00:03:39,702
<i>- This isn't a hoax.</i>

42
00:03:39,805 --> 00:03:41,911
<i>- It's been one full week
since we learned</i>

43
00:03:42,014 --> 00:03:42,877
<i>of their disappearance,</i>

44
00:03:42,981 --> 00:03:45,190
<i>without a new development
in the case,</i>

45
00:03:45,294 --> 00:03:47,227
<i>their friends and family</i>

46
00:03:47,330 --> 00:03:49,436
<i>are starting to fear
the worst.</i>

47
00:03:57,167 --> 00:03:59,377
[picture rustles]

48
00:04:00,309 --> 00:04:02,483
[Mia]: This is Riley,
as you know her,

49
00:04:02,587 --> 00:04:05,383
host of "Paranormal Paranoids."

50
00:04:08,075 --> 00:04:12,528
This is Riley as I know her,
my little sister.

51
00:04:13,149 --> 00:04:15,358
My name is Mia Walker.

52
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:18,499
I've been searching for Riley
for the last 12 years,

53
00:04:19,776 --> 00:04:23,366
and I'd like you to get to know
her the way that I do.

54
00:04:23,470 --> 00:04:29,303
♪ I'm haunted in the morning

55
00:04:30,856 --> 00:04:33,928
[Riley]: One, two,
three, four...

56
00:04:34,032 --> 00:04:37,242
<i>[Mia]: When we were kids,
she was very mature for her age.</i>

57
00:04:37,346 --> 00:04:39,693
<i>She was always thinking,</i>

58
00:04:39,796 --> 00:04:42,661
<i>figuring things out,
seeing things no one else saw.</i>

59
00:04:42,765 --> 00:04:44,560
Some people keep
a dream journal.

60
00:04:44,663 --> 00:04:45,940
Riley kept a dream sketchbook.

61
00:04:46,044 --> 00:04:49,496
<i>She'd start drawing instantly,
as soon as she woke up.</i>

62
00:04:49,599 --> 00:04:51,256
<i>She had extremely vivid dreams.</i>

63
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:54,224
<i>And sometimes...</i>

64
00:04:54,328 --> 00:04:57,573
she even drew her nightmares.

65
00:04:57,676 --> 00:05:00,679
[Riley strumming
guitar continues]

66
00:05:00,783 --> 00:05:02,509
♪ I wonder where I'm falling

67
00:05:02,612 --> 00:05:03,717
<i>[Mia]: In high school,</i>

68
00:05:03,820 --> 00:05:05,960
<i>she started to take the arts
more seriously.</i>

69
00:05:06,064 --> 00:05:08,860
<i>And the Riley that
I knew just melted away</i>

70
00:05:08,963 --> 00:05:11,172
<i>when she was performing.</i>

71
00:05:11,276 --> 00:05:14,417
She really came out
of her shell.

72
00:05:14,521 --> 00:05:17,247
And she got good at that.

73
00:05:17,834 --> 00:05:20,630
<i>Pretending that she was okay
when she wasn't.</i>

74
00:05:21,976 --> 00:05:27,465
♪ Big sister,
won't you find me ♪

75
00:05:27,568 --> 00:05:29,052
<i>[Mia]: So, with that passion
of hers,</i>

76
00:05:29,156 --> 00:05:31,986
<i>it was no surprise
when the channel took off.</i>

77
00:05:32,090 --> 00:05:34,679
[mysterious music plays]

78
00:05:34,782 --> 00:05:37,785
<i>[Jess]: For the last half
of the 20th century,</i>

79
00:05:37,889 --> 00:05:40,581
<i>UFO researchers,
demonologists, psychics,</i>

80
00:05:40,685 --> 00:05:43,377
<i>all that, there was
a mysticism to it.</i>

81
00:05:43,481 --> 00:05:46,000
<i>Even the idea of investigating
the supernatural</i>

82
00:05:46,104 --> 00:05:47,795
<i>was becoming a joke.</i>

83
00:05:49,141 --> 00:05:51,316
What happened with
the Paranoids changed that.

84
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:54,284
- Since then, locals refer
to it simply as

85
00:05:54,388 --> 00:05:56,045
"The Suicide Shed".

86
00:05:56,148 --> 00:05:58,150
<i>[Jess]: YouTube was brand new.</i>

87
00:05:58,254 --> 00:06:00,394
<i>Nobody knew what it could be,
or who might be watching.</i>

88
00:06:00,498 --> 00:06:02,776
<i>The Paranoids tapped
into an audience</i>

89
00:06:02,879 --> 00:06:06,607
<i>that had been relegated
to UFO conventions,</i>

90
00:06:06,711 --> 00:06:08,575
and paranormal chatrooms,

91
00:06:08,678 --> 00:06:10,646
and those people were starved
for content.

92
00:06:10,749 --> 00:06:13,511
<i>[Mia]: Nearly every time
they filmed,</i>

93
00:06:13,614 --> 00:06:15,789
<i>they captured something
most paranormal researchers</i>

94
00:06:15,892 --> 00:06:17,722
<i>spend their entire lives
looking for,</i>

95
00:06:17,998 --> 00:06:20,587
<i>which is why they had
so many doubters.</i>

96
00:06:20,690 --> 00:06:23,175
[ominous music plays]
<i>[Mia]: You know, at first,</i>

97
00:06:23,279 --> 00:06:25,005
<i>I thought they could have been
faking things, sure.</i>

98
00:06:25,108 --> 00:06:27,456
<i>I mean, I didn't know how
else to explain it.</i>

99
00:06:28,249 --> 00:06:32,840
<i>But I also knew that Riley
wouldn't do something like that.</i>

100
00:06:32,944 --> 00:06:35,740
<i>She took all this stuff
very seriously.</i>

101
00:06:35,843 --> 00:06:37,431
[startling bang]
[screaming]

102
00:06:37,535 --> 00:06:38,812
- What was that?

103
00:06:38,915 --> 00:06:42,229
[Laura]: Riley, don't go
all by yourself, Riley.

104
00:06:42,332 --> 00:06:43,920
[Paranoids speaking
indistinctly]

105
00:06:44,024 --> 00:06:45,266
[Laura]: Chill, chill.

106
00:06:45,370 --> 00:06:46,889
[Riley]: Where did
that come from?

107
00:06:46,992 --> 00:06:48,028
[door opens]

108
00:06:48,131 --> 00:06:50,202
[evil growl]

109
00:06:50,306 --> 00:06:52,722
[Paranoids screaming]
- Whoa! Whoa!
- Holy shit!

110
00:06:57,693 --> 00:07:00,489
- I believe
my sister's not a liar.

111
00:07:01,593 --> 00:07:03,802
<i>I tried talking to her about it</i>

112
00:07:03,906 --> 00:07:07,323
<i>but after the prison episode,
she got real quiet.</i>

113
00:07:07,427 --> 00:07:09,912
[footsteps echoing]

114
00:07:18,196 --> 00:07:19,956
- Jesus.

115
00:07:20,060 --> 00:07:21,510
[David]: What?

116
00:07:21,613 --> 00:07:23,546
[breathing nervously]

117
00:07:23,753 --> 00:07:25,410
- Don't you feel that?

118
00:07:25,652 --> 00:07:27,723
[David]: No. Feel what?

119
00:07:28,482 --> 00:07:30,104
- Cold.

120
00:07:32,693 --> 00:07:35,385
[Laura]: Holy shit.
[David]: Oh, fuck!

121
00:07:35,696 --> 00:07:38,941
[Laura]: Riley.
- What? What?

122
00:07:39,044 --> 00:07:40,701
- No, it's fine.
[panicked breathing]

123
00:07:40,805 --> 00:07:42,254
- Wait!
- No, Riley!

124
00:07:42,358 --> 00:07:44,049
Riley!
[Peter]: Riley, no!

125
00:07:44,153 --> 00:07:46,224
- We have to go now!
[ominous music peaks]

126
00:07:47,432 --> 00:07:50,055
<i>[Mia]: A lot of people called
bullshit on that.</i>

127
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:54,612
<i>But then the uploads stopped
and the channel went dark.</i>

128
00:07:54,715 --> 00:07:56,545
Some of the fans were worried,

129
00:07:56,648 --> 00:07:59,271
but most seemed to think it
was a publicity stunt.

130
00:08:00,445 --> 00:08:03,172
<i>And then... everything changed.</i>

131
00:08:03,275 --> 00:08:06,382
- Today's top story, the hosts
of the YouTube channel,

132
00:08:06,486 --> 00:08:10,835
the "Paranormal Paranoids"
have been missing for five days.

133
00:08:11,283 --> 00:08:14,183
<i>[Mia]: People started taking it
seriously after that.</i>

134
00:08:15,322 --> 00:08:16,461
<i>It's sad to say,</i>

135
00:08:16,565 --> 00:08:19,326
<i>but that's really where
their fame began.</i>

136
00:08:19,429 --> 00:08:21,846
<i>After their disappearance,</i>

137
00:08:21,949 --> 00:08:23,399
<i>people all over the world</i>

138
00:08:23,503 --> 00:08:25,056
<i>started scouring through
their videos</i>

139
00:08:25,159 --> 00:08:26,195
<i>searching for answers.</i>

140
00:08:26,298 --> 00:08:28,128
<i>[Fan 1]: There are videos
of her on her channel</i>

141
00:08:28,231 --> 00:08:31,062
<i>talking to someone
offscreen that we've never met.</i>

142
00:08:31,165 --> 00:08:32,512
<i>The police need to be
checking everything.</i>

143
00:08:32,615 --> 00:08:35,031
<i>[Fan 2]: Having clear sight
of a car belonging to a member</i>

144
00:08:35,135 --> 00:08:37,206
<i>of the group may also be helpful
for us going forward,</i>

145
00:08:37,309 --> 00:08:38,966
<i>if we ever need to identify
a vehicle.</i>

146
00:08:39,070 --> 00:08:40,589
<i>[Fan 3]: There were plenty
of theories,</i>

147
00:08:40,692 --> 00:08:42,107
<i>but nothing concrete
ever came forward.</i>

148
00:08:42,211 --> 00:08:44,662
<i>- So, there is a lot
to unpack here.</i>

149
00:08:44,765 --> 00:08:46,146
<i>- And then,
there's this odd clip</i>

150
00:08:46,249 --> 00:08:49,183
of her talking to another
Paranormal Paranoid, Peter.

151
00:08:49,287 --> 00:08:51,910
[mouse clicking]

152
00:08:59,055 --> 00:09:01,713
- Well, we had the gas station
security feed,

153
00:09:01,817 --> 00:09:03,163
and their card numbers.

154
00:09:03,266 --> 00:09:06,062
<i>They had made their last
recorded purchase</i>

155
00:09:06,166 --> 00:09:08,064
<i>there just outside
of Shelby Oaks.</i>

156
00:09:08,168 --> 00:09:12,103
<i>So, we knew they at least
got that far.</i>

157
00:09:12,206 --> 00:09:14,346
Anywhere they kids might
have been going,

158
00:09:14,450 --> 00:09:15,762
we had to investigate.

159
00:09:15,865 --> 00:09:19,179
<i>So, the most obvious place
was the old amusement park.</i>

160
00:09:19,282 --> 00:09:21,491
<i>[people screaming]</i>

161
00:09:21,595 --> 00:09:24,322
<i>[Mia]: It's about
60 miles from here.</i>

162
00:09:24,909 --> 00:09:26,911
<i>My mom used to talk about
it all the time.</i>

163
00:09:27,014 --> 00:09:28,671
<i>She loved going there
when she was a kid.</i>

164
00:09:29,845 --> 00:09:32,433
<i>They had a ballroom and
bands played there.</i>

165
00:09:32,537 --> 00:09:35,126
<i>It was pretty much the reason
to go to Shelby Oaks.</i>

166
00:09:35,229 --> 00:09:36,610
[Ferris wheel clicking]

167
00:09:36,714 --> 00:09:38,129
<i>[Mia]: The park closed
in the late 90s</i>

168
00:09:38,232 --> 00:09:41,650
<i>after a really bad fire.</i>

169
00:09:41,753 --> 00:09:44,687
<i>A lot of people think
the place is haunted.</i>

170
00:09:46,378 --> 00:09:52,039
<i>[Burke]: Shelby Oaks has been
a ghost town since the late 90s.</i>

171
00:09:52,143 --> 00:09:54,973
<i>From the perspective
of these kids, though,</i>

172
00:09:55,077 --> 00:09:58,459
<i>I mean, that place
was a gold mine.</i>

173
00:09:58,943 --> 00:10:04,776
<i>It seemed promising but
it was just another dead end.</i>

174
00:10:06,295 --> 00:10:08,055
- I know this is hard
for people to hear,

175
00:10:08,159 --> 00:10:11,852
but I don't think these are just
going to turn up anything.

176
00:10:11,956 --> 00:10:15,062
<i>I think the energy is better
spent on finding who did it.</i>

177
00:10:15,166 --> 00:10:18,065
<i>[Burke]: Every good cop
knows that feeling.</i>

178
00:10:18,583 --> 00:10:21,310
When it starts to sink in that
the person you're searching for

179
00:10:21,413 --> 00:10:23,381
isn't coming home.

180
00:10:25,245 --> 00:10:30,215
<i>[Mia]: Robert and I met two
years before Riley went missing.</i>

181
00:10:31,009 --> 00:10:32,873
I always wanted to be a mother

182
00:10:32,977 --> 00:10:35,255
and Robert always wanted
to be a daddy.

183
00:10:35,911 --> 00:10:40,916
And we tried for a bit but...
it didn't happen.

184
00:10:42,883 --> 00:10:44,885
<i>And then...</i>

185
00:10:44,989 --> 00:10:46,991
<i>when Riley went missing,</i>

186
00:10:47,094 --> 00:10:49,787
<i>it just...</i>

187
00:10:51,581 --> 00:10:54,343
...it just wasn't the time
anymore.

188
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:56,897
<i>Not after that.</i>

189
00:11:02,903 --> 00:11:05,388
[phone ringing]

190
00:11:38,456 --> 00:11:40,458
[worrying music plays]

191
00:11:57,958 --> 00:12:00,098
<i>[Reporter]: Tragically,
the bodies of Peter Bailey,</i>

192
00:12:00,202 --> 00:12:02,066
<i>Laura Tucker,
and David Reynolds</i>

193
00:12:02,169 --> 00:12:05,310
<i>were found in a cabin just
outside of Shelby Oaks, Ohio,</i>

194
00:12:05,414 --> 00:12:07,278
<i>an abandoned ghost town
the young adults</i>

195
00:12:07,381 --> 00:12:09,659
<i>may have been investigating
for their show,</i>

196
00:12:09,763 --> 00:12:10,971
<i>"Paranormal Paranoids."</i>

197
00:12:11,075 --> 00:12:12,835
<i>On the front door
of the cabin,</i>

198
00:12:12,939 --> 00:12:16,045
<i>this disturbing symbol,
smeared in blood.</i>

199
00:12:16,149 --> 00:12:17,702
<i>Riley Brennan,
the host of the program,</i>

200
00:12:17,806 --> 00:12:19,497
<i>is still missing.</i>

201
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:20,981
- I'm so scared.

202
00:12:21,085 --> 00:12:23,812
<i>[Reporter]: A video camera
was discovered from the scene</i>

203
00:12:23,915 --> 00:12:27,160
<i>that police say may have
captured the perpetrator.</i>

204
00:12:27,885 --> 00:12:29,921
[sinister music]

205
00:12:38,205 --> 00:12:39,275
<i>[Mia]: Once the footage got out,</i>

206
00:12:39,379 --> 00:12:40,449
<i>it sparked a nationwide</i>
campaign.

207
00:12:40,552 --> 00:12:42,485
<i>I mean, you couldn't go
to the grocery store</i>

208
00:12:42,589 --> 00:12:45,005
<i>without seeing it
on a sign or a billboard.</i>

209
00:12:45,109 --> 00:12:47,870
- Who took Riley Brennan?

210
00:12:47,974 --> 00:12:50,217
<i>[Burke]: From the video,
we could ascertain</i>

211
00:12:50,321 --> 00:12:54,912
<i>that the suspect was
a white male, 6'1", maybe 6'2"</i>

212
00:12:55,015 --> 00:12:57,293
<i>based on the height
of the window.</i>

213
00:12:57,397 --> 00:12:59,157
<i>He was wearing gloves.</i>

214
00:12:59,261 --> 00:13:02,643
<i>So, basically we had nothing.</i>

215
00:13:02,747 --> 00:13:04,853
And...

216
00:13:05,646 --> 00:13:07,372
there was uh...

217
00:13:07,476 --> 00:13:09,478
there was that other thing.

218
00:13:12,930 --> 00:13:15,656
<i>We must've watched
that tape 500 times</i>

219
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:18,314
<i>before releasing it
to the public.</i>

220
00:13:18,659 --> 00:13:20,420
<i>None of us saw it.</i>

221
00:13:21,386 --> 00:13:23,803
But now, like...

222
00:13:24,873 --> 00:13:27,082
can't get it outta my head.

223
00:13:28,324 --> 00:13:30,395
[door creaks open]

224
00:13:37,333 --> 00:13:38,818
[footsteps thudding on stairs]

225
00:13:38,921 --> 00:13:41,303
[loud crash]
[Riley]: Oh, God.

226
00:13:41,993 --> 00:13:45,341
[sinister music plays]

227
00:13:51,796 --> 00:13:53,487
<i>[Riley]: Did I ever tell you
about the night terrors</i>

228
00:13:53,591 --> 00:13:54,868
<i>I used to have?</i>

229
00:13:55,869 --> 00:13:59,010
I'd see this man
in my window and...

230
00:14:00,460 --> 00:14:03,187
I just feel trapped.

231
00:14:03,290 --> 00:14:06,121
It's-it's, I mean,
it's weird, it's crazy.

232
00:14:06,224 --> 00:14:08,295
- No, no, you're fine.
- But like, I saw...

233
00:14:08,399 --> 00:14:11,229
like, images of...

234
